From: jempa <jempamartensson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:21:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/43] Deformation motion blur for triangle meshes (for
 hdPbrt)

TriangleMesh can hold a second set of vertex positions (and normals) at the end of a
time interval; vertices move linearly between the two by ray time. trianglemesh takes
"point3 P1" / "normal N1", plymesh "string motionfilename" (a PLY with the same
vertices), both "float motiontimes" [t0 t1]. Triangle bounds cover both poses;
intersection, hit setup and light sampling use the vertices at the ray time; area and
solid angle use the start pose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
